{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548835-ghoul-families-as-bloodlines-of-clan-tzimisce","id":1548835,"title":"Ghoul Families as Bloodlines of Clan Tzimisce","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-02-28T18:57:13-08:00","id":1548835,"title":"Ghoul Families as Bloodlines of Clan Tzimisce","content":"So I got some time over on my hands and decided to make a quick summery of the Ghoul Families as Tzimisce bloodlines. This is very basic with essentially only a Discipline spread and a weakness for each, in addition to the traditional Tzimisce weakness.I can't really pin down why but it felt right that they would have the Tzimisce weakness as a basis to tie them together, along with all of them having Vicissitude as a in-Clan Discipline.<br /> <br /> The main intention is to use them in Dark Ages but they should be useable in the Modern Nights (or Victorian Age for that matter) as well.<br /> <br /> <b>Basarab</b><br /> <u>Disciplines</u>: Dominate, Animalism, Vicissitude<br /> <u>Weakness</u>: Allergic to garlic<br /> <br /> <b>Bratovitch</b><br /> <u>Disciplines:</u> Animalism, Potence, Vicissitude<br /> <u>Weakness:</u> Penalty to all non-Intimidate rolls with non-animals (or creatures with above animal level of sentience)<br /> <br /> <b>Danislavs</b><br /> <u>Disciplines:</u> Auspex, Vicissitude, Celerity<br /> <u>Weakness:</u> Penlty to resist or ride anger frenzy under the full moon<br /> <br /> <b>Grimaldi</b><br /> <u>Disciplines:</u> Fortitude, Presence, Vicissitude<br /> <u>Weakness:</u> -2 points to their max Blood Pool<br /> <br /> <b>Khazi</b><br /> <u>Disciplines: </u>Vicissitude, Obfuscate, Animalism<br /> <u>Weakness:</u> Bashing damage every turn the character is exposed to strong light (full moon, a raging fire, a lantern up close etc.)<br /> <br /> <b>Krevcheski</b><br /> <u>Disciplines:</u> Auspex, Vicissitude, Fortitude<br /> <u>Weakness:</u> Cost for raising social attributes is increased by x2<br /> <br /> <b>Obertus</b><br /> <u>Disciplines:</u> Vicissitude, Obfuscate, Fortitude<br /> <u>Weakness:</u> Derangement (Obsessive)<br /> <br /> <b>Oprichniki</b><br /> <u>Disciplines:</u> Animalism, Vicissitude, Obfuscate<br /> <u>Weakness:</u> Infuriates and strengthen nearby ghosts<br /> <br /> <b>Narov</b><br /> <u>Disciplines</u>: Dominate, Vicissitude, Obfuscate<br /> <u>Weakness</u>: 25% chance of Vitae having no effect if attempts to ghoul, blood bound, sustain a ghoul or Embrace a person<br /> <br /> <b>Ruthvenski</b><br /> <u>Disicplines:</u> Vicissitude, Presence, Celerity<br /> <u>Weakness:</u> Take a bashing damage every round spent inside a home uninvited<br /> <br /> <b>Vlazy</b><br /> <u>Disciplines:</u> Animalism, Fortitude, Vicissitude<br /> <u>Weakness:</u> Must sleep surrounded by a tool of war for every generation from the 14th Generation to restore Willpower. Meaning that a 13th Generation will need one tool of war, a 12th Generation will need two, 11th Generation will need three and so on.<br /> <br /> <b>Szantovich</b><br /> <u>Disciplines:</u> Presence, Potence, Vicissitude<br /> <u>Weakness</u>: Start with a sensual Addicition, like alcohol, drugs, sex or something else in that direction.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-28T20:51:36-08:00","id":1548836,"title":"","content":"Cool. I like how you\u2019ve done that. I actually did something similar a few years back. My versions are slightly different.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Bratovitch</b><br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Animalism, Potence, Vicissitude<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness:</b> Bratovitches are bestial and inhuman in their behavior and even appearance. They suffer a +1 difficulty to all social rolls with humans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Grimaldi</b><br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Celerity, Dominate, Fortitude<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness:</b> The Grimaldi family is less inbred than other Revenant families. This does have its advantages, but the down side is that their blood is less potent. Their maximum blood pools are 2 points lower than they otherwise would be and their Blood Purity score can never exceed 3.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Khavi</b><br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Animalism, Koldunic Sorcery, Vicissitude<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness:</b> The Khavi have pale white skin and hair like that of an albino. This skin carries with it some of the same sensitivity to sunlight that their vampiric progenitors had. Khavi suffer damage from sunlight in the same way that vampires do, though this damage is only bashing and they can soak it with Stamina. Furthermore, while they can change their size and shape with Vicissitude, they can never change the pale white coloration of their flesh or hair. For vampire Khavi, they have the Setite weakness to light.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Obertus</b><br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Obfuscate, Thaumaturgy<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness:</b> The Obertuses were bred for intellectual ability, sometimes at the expense of stability, and are thus prone to monomania and similar psychological disorders. All members of the Obertus family suffer from a single derangement from which they can never recover.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ruthven</b><br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Celerity, Vicissitude*<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness:</b> The Ruthven, for all of their refinement, are contemptuous of those who they see as beneath them and have trouble hiding that contempt. The exact nature of who they dislike varies from Ruthven to Ruthven, but it usually includes a majority of human. It may be races of humanity, those who they see as plebeian or uneducated, might be those who support the wrong sorts of political or philosophical viewpoints. Who ever the targets of their scorn may be, Ruthven have +1 to difficulties to resist frenzy from anger caused by such people and +1 to all difficulties of social rolls to positively influence such people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Vlaszy</b><br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Animalism, Potence, Presence<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness:</b> It is said that the Vlaszy were instilled by their vampiric masters with such a sense of honor that it runs through their very blood even in the modern era. Vlaszy must spend a point of Willpower in order to tell a lie and if one should ever break an oath, that Vlaszy loses a permanent dot of Willpower.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Zantosa</b><br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> Fortitude, Presence, Vicissitude<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness:</b> Zantosas are rather weak-willed when it comes to resisting temptation. Accordingly, whenever a Zantosa is exposed to a particularly pleasurable experience, she must make a Willpower roll (difficulty determined by the Storyteller, depending on the experience in question). Failure indicates that the Zantosa is now obsessed with or addicted to that particular sensation (which can be anything from doing a new drug, to performing a particular sexual position, to enjoying a sumptuous wine, to torturing an unfortunate victim), and will do damn near anything to experience it again.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-28T21:35:28-08:00","id":1548837,"title":"","content":"For my version I gave them all Vicissitude to tie them together into the &quot;Tzimisce family tree&quot; and then wanted weaknesses that had as few openings to interpretation or twisting, or clever sidelining, as possible. I don't know how well I managed with the weaknesses but those were my thoughts when I wrote this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-01T20:04:13-08:00","id":1548861,"title":"","content":"That makes sense. I like how you did a lot of the Bloodlibes. I like the Vlaszy weakness of sleeping with weapons. <br /> <br /> Like you, I also took away Auspex from the Zantosa, though I gave them Fortitude instead. I figured if they were insanely hedonistic and perverse, they would constantly be pushing their bodies to the limit and would become supernaturally tough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-01T20:55:58-08:00","id":1548862,"title":"","content":"Fortitude makes sense for the Zantosa. My reasoning was that I already had three Bloodlines with Fortitude for their physical Discipline so if I also gave Zantosa Fortitude it would be four with that Discipline and just one with Potence. Thus I went with Potence. But thinking things over I could see the Zantosa and Vlazy switch physical Disciplines so that Zantosa gets Fortitude and the Vlazy gets Potence instead of what I've got right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-02T21:16:33-08:00","id":1548895,"title":"","content":"You might be curious to see this old thread of mine. Vicissitude by Revenant family:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/841919-vicissitude-by-revenant-family\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/841919-vicissitude-by-revenant-family\"> Vicissitude by Revenant Family - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/841919-vicissitude-by-revenant-family\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/841919-vicissitude-by-revenant-family </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So, we have talked about Vicissitude house rules before, and I have some more. These are a bit strange because they are based on an alternative setting that my gaming group is working on where Revenant families have a much bigger role in the setting, especially within the Tzimisce Clan. So the nature of a Tzimisce's Vicissitude is going to vary based on the Revenant family that it was born into. Here are some examples for those families which have Vicissitude, I may tweak them further based on my own examination and any input I get from the forums. Zantosa 1. Beyond Pain. The Zantosa push their bodies </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T00:00:15-08:00","id":1548897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1548835-ghoul-families-as-bloodlines-of-clan-tzimisce?p=1548895#post1548895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might be curious to see this old thread of mine. Vicissitude by Revenant family:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/841919-vicissitude-by-revenant-family\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...evenant-family</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Very cool and ambitious. I don't promise anything but I'll try to return later with a longer comment on these versions of Vicissitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}